.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_ITERATOR_SOURCE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_iterator_source
.Nd a flow-controlled source operator
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fo dtfl_iterator_source
.Fa "dtfl_scope *scope"
.Fa "const dtfl_type *type"
.Fa "dtfl_timed_iter_fn next"
.Fa "dtfl_probe *probe"
.Fa "dtfl_ctx ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_iterator_source
builds a source operator in
.Fa scope
that repeatedly calls
.Fa next
to ingest input, holding back while
.Fa probe
is behind the frontier the last ingest targeted.
Each call to
.Fa next
writes the time of its batch into its
.Fa time
argument and emits the batch's records of
.Fa type
through its
.Vt dtfl_emit
handle; it returns
.Dv false
to end the input.
Times chosen by successive calls must be non-decreasing.
.Pp
On each schedule the source ingests while the probe is not behind the
current target, downgrading its capability to each batch's time; when
the probe falls behind the target it reactivates and waits, which
bounds how far the source runs ahead of downstream progress.
The scope's time must be totally ordered.
The caller owns
.Fa probe
and frees it after the computation; the context
.Fa ctx
is released by its destructor when the operator is dropped (PLAN D5).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_iterator_source
returns the source stream, carrying
.Fa type .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_probe *p = dtfl_probe_new();
dtfl_stream *s = dtfl_iterator_source(scope, dtfl_type_u64(),
    read_batch, p, DTFL_NOCTX);
s = dtfl_stream_probe_with(s, p);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_probe_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_to_stream 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
This is the C form of timely's
.Fn iterator_source .
It is public at the pinned release
.Pq Li timely-v0.31.0
and was removed upstream afterward (#818); the port keeps the pinned
behavior.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The stream, the operator and the probe belong to the thread that runs
the worker and must not be used from another thread (PLAN section 5).
